drm/msm/dsi/phy: runtime suspend the PHY in the late system suspend

When the system suspends with the display on, the display is turned off
in the DRM device's .prepare callback. The DSI PLL clocks are unprepared
then and the clock core drops its runtime PM reference on the PHY, but the
PM core already holds one of its own (device_prepare()), so the PHY stays
runtime active and its iface clock prepared. On RPM SoCs that keeps the XO
voted on in the RPM sleep set through s2idle: with the display on at
suspend, APSS never sent the XO sleep vote 0 and the SoC stayed out of VDD
min; with the display already off it reached it (sunstone, SM4375, traced
with a kprobe on qcom_rpm_smd_write()).

Force the PHY into runtime suspend in the late system suspend phase and
restore it in the early resume, when the display is off.

Signed-off-by: 14sea <14sea@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.c
index e0e95a7e8..a57dea60e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy.c
@@ -727,8 +727,15 @@ static int dsi_phy_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	return clk_prepare_enable(phy->ahb_clk);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The display is turned off in the DRM device's .prepare, but by then the PM core holds a runtime
+ * PM reference on the PHY too (device_prepare()), so the clock core's runtime put after the PLL is
+ * unprepared does not suspend the PHY: suspend it late, or the iface clock keeps the XO voted on
+ * through s2idle when the system goes to sleep with the display on.
+ */
 static const struct dev_pm_ops dsi_phy_pm_ops = {
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(dsi_phy_runtime_suspend, dsi_phy_runtime_resume, NULL)
+	SET_LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 };
 
 static struct platform_driver dsi_phy_platform_driver = {
